WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.720
- [Kelly Clarkson] Alright
let's finish this up

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:03.430
with one more single parent story

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.760
proving that you can
be a strong role model

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.180
for your kids all on your own.

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:08.488
This is what I am liking.

00:00:08.488 --> 00:00:11.380
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.840
A mom in New Jersey
recently took the TikTok

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.970
to share her approach with her
19 month old daughter Luna,

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.450
when it comes to explaining
why Luna has one mommy

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.610
and no daddy, take a look.

00:00:21.610 --> 00:00:23.840
- [Mom] So the way I'm raising Luna-

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:24.677
She doesn't want to be in this video.

00:00:24.677 --> 00:00:26.075
You going to say good morning?

00:00:26.075 --> 00:00:27.540
(baby laughing)

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.205
Luna and I are a family
two. A mom and a daughter.

00:00:30.205 --> 00:00:32.100
She wants to play with the video stand.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.130
Some families have one parent,

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.830
some families have two parents.

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.138
A parent can be a mom like Luna and I.

00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:40.229
Mom, baby. Family of two.

00:00:40.229 --> 00:00:43.128
Some families are a mom and a mom.

00:00:43.128 --> 00:00:45.570
Some families are two dads.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.630
Some families might be a mom and a dad.

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.950
You might have a mom and a bonus dad.

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:53.659
Family dynamics in 2021
going onto 2022 almost

00:00:53.659 --> 00:00:57.850
needs to be taught to our
children at the young age.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.670
So as they grow up, it's more normalized.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:01.521
- [Kelly Clarkson] Amen.

00:01:01.521 --> 00:01:02.354
(crowd cheering)

00:01:02.354 --> 00:01:05.090
The video instantly got
tens of thousands of views

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:07.140
and hundreds of parents praising her

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:08.870
for her honesty and awareness.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.090
We have this proud single mama on the line

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.210
watching on NBC for New York at two.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:14.640
What's up Cassie?

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.327
(crowd cheering)

00:01:16.327 --> 00:01:20.648
Hello. Well, first of all,
I grew up in a small town.

00:01:20.648 --> 00:01:21.870
I just have to tell you.

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:24.270
And literally only knew of one other kid

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.230
that had divorced parents.
That there was a different

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:28.120
kind of family scenario going on.

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:30.120
It didn't really happen a lot
in this small town I'm from.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.890
So, you do feel like you're an odd ball,

00:01:32.890 --> 00:01:35.280
like as a kid and like
the daddy daughter dances,

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:36.770
like all that kind of stuff comes up.

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.608
And I think it's so cool what
you're doing and teaching

00:01:38.608 --> 00:01:41.650
at a very young age that
like, there is no norm,

00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:44.740
like everything is a
norm. It's just your norm.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:46.215
So thank you for doing this.

00:01:46.215 --> 00:01:47.048
(crowd cheering)

00:01:47.048 --> 00:01:49.950
Is that kind of why you made the video

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:52.900
just to ensure that like, she
feels like protected safe,

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:54.870
and this is her norm like growing up?

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:57.780
- [Mom] Absolutely. I mean,
single parents are just such

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:01.690
a normal aspect in everyday
life for so many families

00:02:01.690 --> 00:02:03.019
of so many different communities.

00:02:03.019 --> 00:02:05.909
And it's just so important to
get the message out there that

00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:08.160
just because you're a single parent

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.370
and just because that word single

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.417
is in front of your parenthood story,

00:02:12.417 --> 00:02:14.888
doesn't make you any less of a parent.

00:02:14.888 --> 00:02:18.760
And my daughter and I being
a family of two, together,

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:22.240
we are absolutely everything
and single parents can do

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:25.322
absolutely anything and
everything that we want to do.

00:02:25.322 --> 00:02:26.155
(crowd cheering)

00:02:26.155 --> 00:02:27.146
- [Kelly Clarkson] Absolutely

00:02:27.146 --> 00:02:29.271
- [Mom] So that is my biggest one.

00:02:29.271 --> 00:02:30.310
- [Kelly Clarkson] I love it.

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:31.410
So thank you, Cassie.

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:34.120
I'm liking your posts right now, right?

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.680
Oh my God, adorable.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:37.570
She's so adorable.

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:39.900
Well, that's not all our
season long partner Pilot Pen,

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:42.080
the go-to pen of the Kelly
Clarkson show wants to honor

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.090
ultimate overachievers
just like you ma'am.

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:46.470
So they're going to be
using their G2 gelling pen

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:48.360
to write you a check
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:49.347
How does that sound?

00:02:49.347 --> 00:02:50.655
(crowd cheering)

00:02:50.655 --> 00:02:52.557
- [Mom] Oh, what?

00:02:52.557 --> 00:02:53.550
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yeah

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.750
Nice to talk to you girl.

